# DESCRIPTION

p1 drives the SpacemiT P1, the PMIC on the Orange Pi RV2's `i2c8` at address `0x41`, through its I2C controller's bus (k1-i2c(3)).
devmgr(8) starts it by its record after the controller's driver:

```text
driver p1
class power
match dt spacemit,p1
```

It reads and writes the chip's registers as transfers to its address: a register's number written, then its bytes read; or the number and the bytes written.
Its six bucks and eleven LDOs (`aldo1` to `aldo4`, `dldo1` to `dldo7`) each have an enable bit and a voltage code: a buck's from 500 mV to 1.375 V in 5 mV steps, then to 3.475 V in 25 mV steps; an LDO's from 500 mV in 25 mV steps.
The ones its node's `regulators` names are reported and can be switched; one with `regulator-always-on` can't be turned off.
Its real-time clock is read as six binary counts, the second to the year (from 2000), twice alike so no count rolls over between.
`poweroff` sets the chip's shutdown bit, which turns the board off.

# FILES

The tree is served in devmgr(8)'s, at `drivers/p1-dt-pmic@41`, and at `/dev/provider/<service>` in the drivers of the devices its regulators supply.

: `ctl`
  A command a line; it reads empty.
  `on <name>` or `off <name>`, a regulator its node names; `poweroff`.
  A regulator not its node's, `off` for one always on, or a transfer that fails fails the write as invalid, and the driver logs which.
: `status`
  Read only.
  `version 0x<n>`, the chip's; `rtc <date>`, as `2026-11-01T18:04:05Z`, or `unread`; then a line for each regulator its node names, `<name> on|off <microvolts> uV`, and `always-on` where its node says so; then `commands <n>, failed <n>`, and `last failure: <command>: <why>`.

