# BUGS

The real-time clock is only read: it isn't set, its alarm isn't used, and the time service (UTC) doesn't take it. On the Orange Pi RV2 it reads 2000-01-01T00:00:00Z and doesn't count.
A regulator's voltage isn't set, and nothing switches a regulator for the devices it supplies: they run as firmware left them (the SD card's signalling supply, `aldo1`, at 3.3 V).
The PMIC's interrupt, its power key, ADC and GPIOs aren't driven.
